    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for LawDog presents several high-upside opportunities, headlined by **Cal Raleigh** (71.46), whose power profile against a high xERA arm like Ray makes him our most efficient start. **Dylan Beavers** (64.87) and **Masyn Winn** (63.85) also project as elite plays; for **Winn**, the matchup against Rodriguez provides a rare dual-threat edge, with the high-likelihood of a stolen base opportunity against a pitcher with a slow delivery boosting his floor significantly. **Jonathan Aranda** (63.20) and **JJ Bleday** (63.19) are also locked in, with **Bleday** benefiting heavily from a +14% park adjustment that helps neutralize the platoon disadvantage against Feltner.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Tyler Freeman**, who flirted with a start but ultimately fell to 46.75 due to a stifling matchup against the elite Greene. While **Freeman** offers positional versatility, the optimizer prioritized the higher projected offensive output of **Geraldo Perdomo** (61.86), whose spot at the top of the lineup remains a catalyst for our Roto categories. We remain cautious with **Bryce Harper** (58.88); while his talent is undeniable, facing a 3.49 xERA pitcher like McLean dampens his daily ceiling compared to the value we are extracting from the bottom of our lineup. \n\nPlease note that **Ryan Waldschmidt** remains a marginal start (47.44) due to his #9 position in the order; monitor the official lineup closely, as any shift upward would immediately elevate his utility. While the rest of the roster is set, keep an eye on the health status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains on the IL, and ensure no weather-related delays impact the high-ceiling matchups we are exploiting today.",
